The residual trajectory is a textbook fast linear convergence (contraction ratio **~0.035**/iteration): cold start from 330 K needs 5 iterations (43.7 K → 1.5 K → 5e-2 → 1.9e-3 → 6.7e-5), noise floor ~6.7e-5 K — well below `tol_T10=1e-4`. Key insight: the inner loop is *not* the bottleneck (only 5 iterations); the cost is **~15 s per inner iteration** = 5-6 `estado_de` inversions at ~2.4-3.2 s each. With warm start (fixed point only moves ~2 K between outer evals), the inner loop needs ~2-3 iterations instead of 5 → ~40% cut per evaluation. Tolerance `tol_T10=1e-4` sits only 1.5× above the measured noise floor → a documented relaxation to 1e-3 is defensible and saves ~1 iteration/eval.

